  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/f1bf8cde-a8e7-4144-9ad6-5d071fc3f7cf.png\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 200px;\" /><br />Foot of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on line <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1,1</mn></mfenced></math><br />Because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>0,0</mn></mfenced></math> divides <math><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Hence, by using section formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Slope of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br />Equation of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
